Improved touch-button behavior so held presses no longer trigger wildly fast changes.
Fixed the underlying debounce bug where the UI refresh was resetting the touch timer and letting repeat presses continue too quickly.
Added safe default EEPROM values for brand-new boards so settings initialize consistently instead of using random erased memory.
Set the default temp delay to 30 minutes and initialized temp min/max defaults cleanly on first boot.
Reduced unnecessary writes by only updating min/max temperature values when they actually change.
Stopped the status screen from redrawing temp min/max every cycle when the values have not changed.
Improved the firmware’s manual cycle logic so the cycle screen and main run state operate more independently.
Updated button and screen interactions to make the UI behavior clearer and more reliable.
Added a safer abort flow so punches can be cancelled and the actuator reset/shake sequence completes before new activity begins.
Continued the refactor to modularize the firmware and make the code easier to maintain and reason about.